s=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">4</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">5</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">5</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">3</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\"><span class=\"delimsizing size3\">)</span></span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:11.5401em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mopen\">{</span><span class=\"mclose\">}</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:18.3501em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:37.2003em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-18.3501em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:20.8501em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:20.8501em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.1em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:20.8501em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-12.1001em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:20.8501em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-20.5001em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:20.8501em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-21.7001em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:20.8501em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-24.1002em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:20.8501em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-30.1002em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:20.8501em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-38.5003em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:20.8501em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-39.7003em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:20.8501em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:18.3501em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[39]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|}\\hline\\text{rep} & \\text{mu} & \\text{irreps missed}\\\\\\hline\\text{[3,1,0]} & \\left\\{\\left\\{1\\right\\},\\left\\{0,0\\right\\}\\right\\} & \\begin{pmatrix}3 & 3 & 2\\\\4 & 2 & 2\\\\4 & 3 & 1\\\\4 & 4 & 0\\\\5 & 2 & 1\\\\5 & 3 & 0\\\\6 & 1 & 1\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{[3,1,0]} & \\left\\{\\left\\{1\\right\\},\\left\\{1,1\\right\\}\\right\\} & \\begin{pmatrix}3 & 3 & 2\\\\4 & 2 & 2\\\\4 & 3 & 1\\\\4 & 4 & 0\\\\5 & 3 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{[3,1,0]} & \\left\\{\\left\\{2\\right\\},\\left\\{1,1\\right\\}\\right\\} & \\begin{pmatrix}3 & 3 & 2\\\\4 & 4 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{[3,1,0]} & \\left\\{\\left\\{3\\right\\},\\left\\{1,1\\right\\}\\right\\} & \\{\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{[3,2,0]} & \\left\\{\\left\\{2\\right\\},\\left\\{0,0\\right\\}\\right\\} & \\begin{pmatrix}4 & 3 & 3\\\\4 & 4 & 2\\\\5 & 3 & 2\\\\5 & 4 & 1\\\\5 & 5 & 0\\\\6 & 2 & 2\\\\6 & 3 & 1\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{[3,2,0]} & \\left\\{\\left\\{2\\right\\},\\left\\{1,1\\right\\}\\right\\} & \\begin{pmatrix}4 & 3 & 3\\\\4 & 4 & 2\\\\5 & 3 & 2\\\\5 & 5 & 0\\\\6 & 2 & 2\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{[3,2,0]} & \\left\\{\\left\\{2\\right\\},\\left\\{2,2\\right\\}\\right\\} & \\begin{pmatrix}4 & 3 & 3\\\\5 & 5 & 0\\end{pmatrix}\\\\\\hline\\text{[3,2,0]} & \\left\\{\\left\\{3\\right\\},\\left\\{2,2\\right\\}\\right\\} & \\{\\}\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "e277bec7-9899-45e4-84f9-f940a81d215b"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings: irrep reach (2026-09-29, point 1, $w=(7/3,-1/2,4)$, generic $k$, exact)\n\n| rep | operator on $\\langle v_g|$ (one-body) | irreps missed |\n|---|---|---|\n| $[3,1,0]$ | $1$ | all but $[6,2,0]$ |\n| | $t_{11}$ | $[3,3,2],[4,2,2],[4,3,1],[4,4,0],[5,3,0]$ |\n| | $\\tfrac{T_{20}}{T_{10}}t_{11}$ ($=R\\,t_{11}$) | $[3,3,2],[4,4,0]$ |\n| | $\\tfrac{T_{30}}{T_{10}}t_{11}$ | **none** |\n| $[3,2,0]$ | $1$ | all but $[6,4,0]$ |\n| | $t_{11}$ | $[4,3,3],[4,4,2],[5,3,2],[5,5,0],[6,2,2]$ |\n| | $T_{22}$ | $[4,3,3],[5,5,0]$ |\n| | $\\tfrac{T_{30}}{T_{20}}T_{22}$ | **none** |\n\nThe top SoV-basis operator $O_{\\{\\{\\lambda_1\\},\\{\\lambda_2,\\lambda_2\\}\\}}=\\mathbb T_{\\lambda_1,0}\\mathbb T_{\\lambda_2,0}^{-1}\\mathbb T_{\\lambda_2,\\lambda_2}(\\theta_1)$ is one-body on the twist-$w$ vacuum and reaches every irrep of $\\Lambda\\otimes\\Lambda$ for both reps, closing the $[3,1,0]$ gap ($[3,3,2],[4,4,0]$) with full transfer matrices only.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## More data points\nVary the point $(h,\\theta,z)$, the vacuum twist $w$ and the generic group element $k$ used in the irrep test. Point 2 is the one from main-notes; point 3 is new.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[setPoint2, irrepDataK, reachTestK, cfgRun];\n(* chain twist = companion of z; memoised monodromies depend on h, theta, so wipe them *)\nsetPoint2[p_] := (hh = p[\"h\"]; th = p[\"th\"]; Gz = companion[p[\"z\"]]; clearMemo /@ {Tu, TGm, tMat};);\npts = <|1 -> <|\"h\" -> 1/3, \"th\" -> {2/7, -5/11}, \"z\" -> {2, -3, 5}|>, 2 -> <|\"h\" -> 1/2, \"th\" -> {3/13, -4/17}, \"z\" -> {3, -7/2, 11/4}|>, 3 -> <|\"h\" -> 2/7, \"th\" -> {1/5, -3/4}, \"z\" -> {-2, 7/3, 3/2}|>|>;\nkPars = <|1 -> {2/3, -1/2, 3/5, -1/4, 2/7, 1/3}, 2 -> {-3/4, 5/6, -2/5, 3/7, -1/3, 4/9}|>;\nirrepDataK[rep_, kp_] := Module[{d = dim[rep], E, EEr, wts, raise, doms, kmat},\n   E[i_, j_] := SparseArray[JJ[i, j, rep]];\n   EEr[i_, j_] := KroneckerProduct[E[i, j], IdentityMatrix[d, SparseArray]] + KroneckerProduct[IdentityMatrix[d, SparseArray], E[i, j]];\n   wts = Transpose[Diagonal /@ Table[Normal[EEr[i, i]], {i, 3}]];\n   raise = Join[EEr[1, 2], EEr[2, 3]];\n   doms = Select[Union[wts], #[[1]] >= #[[2]] >= #[[3]] &];\n   kmat = MatrixExp[kp[[1]] JJ[2, 1, rep] + kp[[2]] JJ[3, 1, rep] + kp[[3]] JJ[3, 2, rep]] . MatrixExp[kp[[4]] JJ[1, 2, rep] + kp[[5]] JJ[1, 3, rep] + kp[[6]] JJ[2, 3, rep]];\n   <|\"hw\" -> Select[Association@Table[With[{idx = Flatten@Position[wts, mu]}, mu -> (Normal[SparseArray[Thread[idx -> #], d^2]] & /@ NullSpace[Normal[raise[[All, idx]]]])], {mu, doms}], # =!= {} &], \"Pik\" -> KroneckerProduct[kmat, kmat]|>];\n(* labels: All, or an explicit list (e.g. just O_max); returns {label, one-body?, missed irreps} *)\nreachTestK[rep_, w_, kp_, labsIn_] := Module[{s2, vW, lsf, ird, labs, oneBody},\n   setRep2[rep];\n   s2 = lwVec[rep] . gRot[rep, rFromW[w]]; vW = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[s2, s2]];\n   lsf = LinearSolve[Transpose[tLamMat[Gz][{rep[[2]], 0}, th[[1]]]]];\n   ird = irrepDataK[rep, kp];\n   labs = If[labsIn === All, gtLabels[rep], labsIn];\n   oneBody[x_] := With[{m = Select[ArrayReshape[Normal[x], {d2, d2}], Max[Abs[#]] > 0 &]}, m =!= {} && MatrixRank[Append[m, s2]] == 1];\n   Table[With[{x = opVec[vW, lsf][lab]}, {lab, oneBody[x], If[oneBody[x], Keys@Select[reachOf[x, ird], # == 0 &], \"-\"]}], {lab, labs}]];\n(* configuration = {point, w, k}; also checks the vacuum is twist-w eigen *)\ncfgRun[rep_, {pt_, w_, kk_}, labs_] := (setPoint2[pts[pt]]; setRep2[rep]; <|\"rep\" -> rep, \"cfg\" -> {pt, w, kk}, \"vacEigen\" -> vacCheck[w], \"rows\" -> Select[reachTestK[rep, w, kPars[kk], labs], #[[2]] &]|>);\ncfgs = {{2, {7/3, -1/2, 4}, 1}, {1, {-5/2, 3, 1/5}, 2}, {3, {11/3, -2, 5/7}, 2}, {2, {-5/2, 3, 1/5}, 1}};",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Modular version for $[4,2,0]$\nExact LU of the dense $729\\times729$ rational $\\mathbb T_{2,0}(\\theta_1)$ takes minutes. Everything is built exactly, then reduced mod a large prime $p$; the solve and all rank tests are done mod $p$ (ranks agree with $\\mathbb Q$ except with negligible probability; two primes used). Validated on $[3,1,0]$, $[3,2,0]$ against the exact runs.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[modP, modPS, reachTestP, cfgRunP];\n(* rational -> Z/p, elementwise; sparse version keeps the pattern *)\nmodP[a_, p_] := Mod[Numerator[a] PowerMod[Denominator[a], -1, p], p];\nSetAttributes[modP, Listable];\nmodPS[s_SparseArray, p_] := SparseArray[Thread[s[\"NonzeroPositions\"] -> modP[s[\"NonzeroValues\"], p]], Dimensions[s]];\nreachTestP[rep_, w_, kp_, labsIn_, p_] := Module[{s2, s2p, vW, denT, ird, hwP, PikP, labs, oneBody, xp, reachP},\n   setRep2[rep];\n   s2 = lwVec[rep] . gRot[rep, rFromW[w]]; s2p = modP[s2, p]; vW = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[s2, s2]];\n   denT = modPS[Transpose[SparseArray[tLamMat[Gz][{rep[[2]], 0}, th[[1]]]]], p];\n   ird = irrepDataK[rep, kp];\n   PikP = modP[Normal[ird[\"Pik\"]], p]; hwP = Map[modP[#, p] &, ird[\"hw\"], {2}];\n   labs = If[labsIn === All, gtLabels[rep], labsIn];\n   (* numerator exactly, then solve y . T_{l2,0} = x mod p *)\n   xp[lab : {{m11_}, {m21_, m12_}}] := LinearSolve[denT, modP[Normal[tLamAct[Gz][{m11, 0}, th[[1]]][tLamAct[Gz][{m21, m12}, th[[1]]][vW]]], p], Modulus -> p];\n   oneBody[x_] := With[{m = Select[ArrayReshape[x, {d2, d2}], Max[#] > 0 &]}, m =!= {} && MatrixRank[Append[m, s2p], Modulus -> p] == 1];\n   reachP[x_] := Map[MatrixRank[{Mod[Mod[x . PikP, p] . Transpose[#], p]}, Modulus -> p] &, hwP];\n   Table[With[{x = xp[lab]}, {lab, oneBody[x], If[oneBody[x], Keys@Select[reachP[x], # == 0 &], \"-\"]}], {lab, labs}]];\ncfgRunP[rep_, {pt_, w_, kk_}, labs_, p_] := (setPoint2[pts[pt]]; setRep2[rep]; <|\"rep\" -> rep, \"cfg\" -> {pt, w, kk}, \"p\" -> p, \"rows\" -> Select[reachTestP[rep, w, kPars[kk], labs, p], #[[2]] &]|>);\nprimes = {NextPrime[10^9], NextPrime[2 10^9]};",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* checks run (~25 s per [4,2,0] config): mod-p reproduces exact [3,1,0],[3,2,0]; all configs x primes give identical rows *)\nbase420 = cfgRunP[{4, 2, 0}, {1, {7/3, -1/2, 4}, 1}, All, primes[[1]]][\"rows\"];\nGrid[Prepend[{#[[1]], #[[3]]} & /@ base420, {\"mu (one-body on twist-w vacuum)\", \"irreps of [4,2,0]^2 missed\"}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
