  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[genericCheck];\n(* does T_{n,0}T_{l2,l2} = T_{l2,0}T_{n,l2} hold away from th1?  Also: is the difference at generic u proportional to T_{n,l2,1}(u) t_3-type terms?  Report which shifted quantum determinants t_3(th1 + k h) vanish on this rep *)\ngenericCheck[rep_, pt_, n_, u_] := Module[{l2 = rep[[2]], D},\n   setPoint2[pts[pt]]; setRep2[rep];\n   D = Normal[tLamMat[Gz][{n, 0}, u] . tLamMat[Gz][{l2, l2}, u] - tLamMat[Gz][{l2, 0}, u] . tLamMat[Gz][{n, l2}, u]];\n   {rep, n, u, D === 0 D, If[D === 0 D, \"-\", MatrixRank[{Flatten[D], Flatten[Normal[tLamMat[Gz][{n, l2, 1}, u]]]}] == 1]}];\nqdetZeros[rep_, pt_] := (setPoint2[pts[pt]]; setRep2[rep]; Select[Range[-3, 3], Normal[tMat[Gz][3][th[[1]] + # hh]] === 0 Normal[tMat[Gz][3][th[[1]]]] &]);\ngc = {genericCheck[{2, 1, 0}, 1, 2, 3/11], genericCheck[{3, 1, 0}, 1, 3, 3/11], genericCheck[{3, 1, 0}, 1, 3, th[[1]] + 1/1000]};\n{Grid[Prepend[gc, {\"rep\", \"n\", \"u\", \"identity holds\", \"difference ~ T_{n,l2,1}(u)?\"}], Frame -> All], \"k with t3(th1+k h)=0, [3,1,0] (two-site)\" -> qdetZeros[{3, 1, 0}, 1]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
