  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Findings: the ratio operators are polynomial (2026-09-29, exact)\n\n**Operator identity at $\\theta_1$** (full two-site space, chain twist $G_c(z)$, no vacuum needed):\n$$\\mathbb T_{n,0}(\\theta_1)\\,\\mathbb T_{\\lambda_2,\\lambda_2}(\\theta_1)=\\mathbb T_{\\lambda_2,0}(\\theta_1)\\,\\mathbb T_{n,\\lambda_2}(\\theta_1)\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\mathbb T_{n,0}\\mathbb T_{\\lambda_2,0}^{-1}\\mathbb T_{\\lambda_2,\\lambda_2}(\\theta_1)=\\mathbb T_{n,\\lambda_2}(\\theta_1),$$\nwith coefficient **exactly 1**. Checked for $[2,1,0]$ ($n=1,2$), $[3,1,0]$ ($n=1,2,3$) and $[3,2,0]$ ($n=2,3$) at points 1 and 2. So $O_{\\max}=\\mathbb T_{\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2}(\\theta_1)$, the transfer matrix in the site rep itself. In particular $R\\,t_{11}=\\mathbb T_{2,1}(\\theta_1)$ (the adjoint singlet-reaching operator), and $\\tfrac{T_{30}}{T_{10}}t_{11}=\\mathbb T_{3,1}(\\theta_1)$.\n\n- The shift is exactly $s=0$. For $s=-3,\\dots,3$, $s\\neq0$, $\\mathbb T_{3,1}(\\theta_1+sh)$ fails both as an operator and on the vacuum.\n- The identity is special to $\\theta_1$. It fails at $u=3/11$ and at $u=\\theta_1+10^{-3}$. At $\\theta_1$ the two-site $t_3(\\theta_1)=t_3(\\theta_1+2h)=0$ ($[3,1,0]$).\n- At generic $u$, the difference is **not** of the form $c\\,t_3(u+ah)\\,\\mathbb T_{n-1,\\lambda_2-1}(u+bh)$, for $a=0..2$, $b=-1..2$. Its exact form (a Jacobi–Trudi/Plücker-type relation) is open.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Multiplicity coverage for $[2,1,0]^{\\otimes2}$ (span question)\nAfter undoing the global $g$, each one-body covector is $\\langle v|\\otimes\\langle\\mathrm{lw}|$ with $v=a\\,g^{-1}$. Question: do the covectors from $1,\\ t_{11},\\ Rt_{11}=\\mathbb T_{2,1}(\\theta_1)$ (over several twists $w$) cover the full multiplicity space of every irrep, in particular $8^{\\oplus2}$? Test: for irrep $\\rho$ with copies $\\mathrm{hw}_a$, the matrix $N_{(X,k),a}=\\langle X|\\Pi(k)|\\mathrm{hw}_a\\rangle$ over several generic $k$ has rank $=$ multiplicity iff the covectors separate all copies. (The earlier reach test used one $k$ and one $X$, so its rank was at most 1 by construction.) Benchmark: all of $V\\otimes\\langle\\mathrm{lw}|$ ($e_i\\otimes\\mathrm{lw}$, $i=1..8$), which must give full multiplicity (PRV).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "ClearAll[multTest];\n(* several generic group elements k, so that a single covector can already see several copies *)\nkList = {{2/3, -1/2, 3/5, -1/4, 2/7, 1/3}, {-3/4, 5/6, -2/5, 3/7, -1/3, 4/9}, {1/5, 2/9, -5/7, 6/11, -1/6, 3/8}, {-2/3, 1/4, 4/5, -3/7, 5/9, -2/11}};\n(* rank of N_{(X,k),a} per irrep, for a list of two-site covectors Xs *)\nrankOfK[Xs_, irds_] := Association@Table[rho -> MatrixRank[Flatten[Table[((x . ird[\"Pik\"]) . #) & /@ ird[\"hw\"][rho], {x, Xs}, {ird, irds}], 1]], {rho, Keys[irds[[1]][\"hw\"]]}];\nmultTest[rep_, pt_, ws_, labs_] := Module[{lsf, irds, data, lw},\n   setPoint2[pts[pt]]; setRep2[rep]; lw = lwVec[rep];\n   lsf = LinearSolve[Transpose[tLamMat[Gz][{rep[[2]], 0}, th[[1]]]]];\n   irds = irrepDataK[rep, #] & /@ kList;\n   data = Flatten[Table[Module[{g = gRot[rep, rFromW[w]], gi, s2, vW, X, m, j0, v},\n       gi = Inverse[g]; s2 = lw . g; vW = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[s2, s2]];\n       X = Normal@opVec[vW, lsf][lab]; m = ArrayReshape[X, {d2, d2}]; j0 = First@FirstPosition[s2, x_ /; x != 0];\n       v = (m[[All, j0]]/s2[[j0]]) . gi;\n       (* undoing g globally must give exactly v (x) lw *)\n       <|\"lab\" -> lab, \"w\" -> w, \"undo g = v x lw\" -> (X . KroneckerProduct[gi, gi] === Flatten[KroneckerProduct[v, lw]]), \"X\" -> X, \"v\" -> v|>], {w, ws}, {lab, labs}], 1];\n   <|\"mult\" -> (Length /@ irds[[1]][\"hw\"]),\n    \"all undo-g checks\" -> And @@ data[[All, \"undo g = v x lw\"]],\n    \"per op, one w\" -> Table[lab -> rankOfK[{First[Select[data, #[\"lab\"] === lab &]][\"X\"]}, irds], {lab, labs}],\n    \"per op, all w\" -> Table[lab -> rankOfK[Select[data, #[\"lab\"] === lab &][[All, \"X\"]], irds], {lab, labs}],\n    \"union, all\" -> rankOfK[data[[All, \"X\"]], irds],\n    \"site-1 span dim of v's\" -> MatrixRank[data[[All, \"v\"]]],\n    \"benchmark V x lw\" -> rankOfK[Table[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[UnitVector[d2, i], lw]], {i, d2}], irds]|>];\nlabs210 = {{{1}, {0, 0}}, {{1}, {1, 1}}, {{2}, {1, 1}}}; (* 1, t11, R t11 = T21(th1) *)\nwsList = {{7/3, -1/2, 4}, {-5/2, 3, 1/5}, {11/3, -2, 5/7}};\nmt210 = multTest[{2, 1, 0}, 1, wsList, labs210];\nmtGrid[mt_] := Grid[Join[{{\"\", Sequence @@ Keys[mt[\"mult\"]]}, {\"multiplicity\", Sequence @@ Values[mt[\"mult\"]]}},\n    {\"one w: \" <> ToString[#[[1]]], Sequence @@ Values[#[[2]]]} & /@ mt[\"per op, one w\"],\n    {\"3 w: \" <> ToString[#[[1]]], Sequence @@ Values[#[[2]]]} & /@ mt[\"per op, all w\"],\n    {{\"union all\", Sequence @@ Values[mt[\"union, all\"]]}, {\"benchmark V x lw\", Sequence @@ Values[mt[\"benchmark V x lw\"]]}}], Frame -> All];\n{mtGrid[mt210], \"undo-g checks\" -> mt210[\"all undo-g checks\"], \"site-1 span\" -> mt210[\"site-1 span dim of v's\"]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"144407\" data-output-id=\"0\" data-out-n=\"62\" data-sub-idx=\"10\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"32\" data-sub-start=\"29\" data-sub-end=\"29\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[62]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-line-broken=\"1\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:13.84em;vertical-align:-6.67em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"col-align-r\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.17em;\"><span style=\"top:-9.17em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.29em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.28em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.29em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.67em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"col-align-l\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:7.17em;\"><span style=\"top:-9.17em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.29em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen\"><span class=\"delimsizing mult\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.25em;\"><span style=\"top:-1.366em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.216em;\"></span><span class=\"delimsizinginner